  "notes": "Transcribed from the official SCC 'Economics AA-T Degree' program map, Catalog 2026-27, published September 22, 2026 (mapmaker.losrios.edu/Maps/7542/PublishedPdf). GE Pattern: Cal-GETC. Associate Degree for Transfer (ADT). Official Total Units: 60-65; this seed models the first-listed/recommended path = 16+16+16+14 = 62 units. Semester sums verified against the map's 16-17 / 16 / 15-17 / 13-15 headers. Choice slots: (1) STAT C1000 / STAT C1000H (Introduction to Statistics); (2) ENGL C1000 / ENGL 488 / ESLW 340 (Honors) — ENGL C1000 at 3 units per the official SCC English course page; (3) INDIS 313 / HCD 310 — first-time college students take INDIS 313 per FYE advising note; (4) Major Elective (minimum 6 units; one course per semester not already completed): ACCT 301, ACCT 311, CISC 310, CISP 360, MATH 355, MATH 372, MATH 401, MATH 402, MATH 410 — this path uses ACCT 301 (Sem 3) then ACCT 311 (Sem 4; requires ACCT 301 with 'C' or better, in-plan). Placement/prior-coursework prereqs (documented, not in prereq arrays): MATH 400 requires MATH 372 & MATH 373, or MATH 375, or MATH 386 with 'C' or better, or placement (MATHS 60/MATH 400 combo for students not placing directly in); students not placing directly in STAT C1000 take the STAT 10/STAT C1000 combo; students not placing directly in ENGL C1000 take the ENGL 80/ENGL C1000 combo. Advising notes: Cal-GETC Area 4 requires 2 courses from different disciplines — the Sem 1 Area 4 GE course must be in a discipline other than ECON; Area 5C lab component not required if a laboratory activity is included in 5A or 5B. Electives: any courses numbered 300-499 (see counselor). ADT requirements: all major courses with 'C' or better; 60 CSU-transferable units (12 within Los Rios); Cal-GETC Areas 1-6 with 'C' or better. tccns mirrors SCC local course codes (California community colleges do not use TCCNS).",
